# API Information


main: {
  kit: {
    info: {
      contact: {
        name: "Proxmint support"
        url: "https://proxmint.com/contact"
      }
      description: `Two kinds of endpoint. The free proxy list and IP geolocation are open and key-free: rate limited per IP and sent with \`access-control-allow-origin: *\`, so they work from a browser as well as a server. The proxy list is published under CC BY 4.0 — attribution is the only condition.

The customer API under \`/api/v1\` is read-only and needs an API key, created under Settings in the dashboard and sent as \`Authorization: Bearer <key>\`. It returns proxy credentials, so it sends no CORS headers: call it from a server, never from browser code.`
      license: {
        name: "CC BY 4.0"
        url: "https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/"
      }
      security: {
        in: "header"
        name: "Authorization"
        prefix: "Bearer"
        scheme: "apiKey"
        type: "http"
      }
      servers: [
        {
          url: "https://proxmint.com"
        }
      ]
      summary: "Free proxy list and IP geolocation with no key; read-only account data with one."
      title: "Proxmint API"
      version: "1.1.0"
      website: "https://proxmint.com"
    }
  }
}

